Subject: Keep the frame's position across a fused property read

What this does
  Keep the frame's position across a fused property read.

Why we need it
  `ROP_get_arg_field`/`ROP_get_local_field` (the fused `get_loc(n) get_field` pair) call `JS_GetProperty`, which can run a getter, but they never published the frame's position the way `ROP_get_field` does. A getter that throws therefore produced a backtrace frame with `(missing)` where the stack build named the line of the read -- seen whenever the receiver load is fused, which the baseline tier does for every property read (the `readX` frame of `accessor-throw-stack.js`).

What it adds
  The monolith threaded labels, the `regvm_exec_one` arms and the generated threaded twins all capture `i_start` before the slow read and call `REGVM_CAPTURE_IP_MONO`; `quickjs-regvm-step.inc` is regenerated.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
diff --git a/quickjs-regvm-step.inc b/quickjs-regvm-step.inc
index a1e3023..20cdc6e 100644
--- a/quickjs-regvm-step.inc
+++ b/quickjs-regvm-step.inc
@@ -2560,6 +2560,10 @@ static uint8_t *REGVM_CC regvm_s_ROP_get_local_field(uint8_t *ip, JSValue *fr, J
                     SET_REG_B(d, val);
                     REGVM_NEXT();
                 }
+                /* A slow read may run a getter that throws; the fused receiver
+                   read has no separate get_field to capture this frame's line.
+                   */
+                REGVM_CAPTURE_IP_MONO(i_start);
                 if (site == REG_IC_NONE)
                     val = JS_GetProperty(ctx, recv, atom);
                 else
@@ -2597,6 +2601,10 @@ static uint8_t *REGVM_CC regvm_s_ROP_get_local_field_0(uint8_t *ip, JSValue *fr,
                     SET_REG_B(d, val);
                     REGVM_NEXT();
                 }
